(622858, 64592, 2333, '<td valign="top">Beautiful model; very nice, natural pose. Good exposure; light from front could be softer, the sharp shadows of the hat and of the flower against her wrist are a bit distracting.. It could benefit from levels (bring in white point) &amp; a slight contrast boost.</td>', 'Beautiful model; very nice, natural pose. Good exposure; light from front could be softer, the sharp shadows of the hat and of the flower against her wrist are a bit distracting.. It could benefit from levels (bring in white point) & a slight contrast boost.', '2004-03-15 20:49:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(622859, 64561, 6667, '<td valign="top">Defiinitely different!  BOL</td>', 'Defiinitely different!  BOL', '2004-03-15 20:50:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(622860, 64592, 6667, '<td valign="top">I''m in love again!  The hat does it everytime!  Nicely done. BOL</td>', 'I''m in love again!  The hat does it everytime!  Nicely done. BOL', '2004-03-15 20:52:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(622861, 64626, 2333, '<td valign="top">I like the pose and the choice of B+W, don''t care for the sunglasses, it would be nice to see her eyes. Not completely sure about the tree behind him, perhaps a bit more physical separation to throw it a bit more OOF.</td>', 'I like the pose and the choice of B+W, don''t care for the sunglasses, it would be nice to see her eyes. Not completely sure about the tree behind him, perhaps a bit more physical separation to throw it a bit more OOF.', '2004-03-15 20:53:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(622862, 64543, 6388, '<td valign="top">I don''t suppose I''ll be the only one to say it, but this one could have done without the blue eyes and the translucent border.  Both are tricks that average photographers use to try to fool the viewer into thinking it''s something unique.  well friend - this picture didn''t need that.  aside from those effects, it''s absolutely perfect.  she''s just an angel with loads of camera appeal.  the technicals of the phots are great as well; soft lighting, no harsh shadows, nice desaturation, nice crop...and that grin!  awesome.  it won''t score as well as it should have.  make this into a regular duotone and frame it proudly.<br/>(no offense intended - just shooting from the hip)<br/>Pedro</td>', 'I don''t suppose I''ll be the only one to say it, but this one could have done without the blue eyes and the translucent border.  Both are tricks that average photographers use to try to fool the viewer into thinking it''s something unique.  well friend - this picture didn''t need that.  aside from those effects, it''s absolutely perfect.  she''s just an angel with loads of camera appeal.  the technicals of the phots are great as well; soft lighting, no harsh shadows, nice desaturation, nice crop...and that grin!  awesome.  it won''t score as well as it should have.  make this into a regular duotone and frame it proudly.(no offense intended - just shooting from the hip)Pedro', '2004-03-15 20:53:25.000000', NULL, 1),
