(628272, 64370, 6388, '<td valign="top">don''t love the yella teddy bear bro, but love the lighting and the grin.  is that with the 550?  very gentle lighting, and doesn''t look to be a lot of post processing.  good job.<br/>Pedro<br/>ps is that a flames hat?</td>', 'don''t love the yella teddy bear bro, but love the lighting and the grin.  is that with the 550?  very gentle lighting, and doesn''t look to be a lot of post processing.  good job.Pedrops is that a flames hat?', '2004-03-19 03:00:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(628274, 64593, 6388, '<td valign="top">um...yes.  The always lovely Anastasia looks justa bout perfect - lighting, tones, depth, and of course...genetics :)<br/>Best pure portrait in the challenge I''d say.<br/>Pedro</td>', 'um...yes.  The always lovely Anastasia looks justa bout perfect - lighting, tones, depth, and of course...genetics :)Best pure portrait in the challenge I''d say.Pedro', '2004-03-19 03:02:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(628275, 64485, 6388, '<td valign="top">pretty flat duotone - the exposed parts wash out.  I''ve seen that with a few in this challenge, and it seems to me to be the ones that use channel mixer to convert to greyscale.  that method usually overdoes the red, so it doesn''t give much contrast in the lighter parts.  Either way, a little more contrast and this improves a ton in my eyes.  good concept, and clean hue shift in the eyes.<br/>Pedro</td>', 'pretty flat duotone - the exposed parts wash out.  I''ve seen that with a few in this challenge, and it seems to me to be the ones that use channel mixer to convert to greyscale.  that method usually overdoes the red, so it doesn''t give much contrast in the lighter parts.  Either way, a little more contrast and this improves a ton in my eyes.  good concept, and clean hue shift in the eyes.Pedro', '2004-03-19 03:05:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(628277, 64574, 6388, '<td valign="top">get her to take three steps away from the backdrop and get a backlight in there, and this is great.  a little space and shallow depth would separate her a bit, and i think that would be a plus, as well as losing some of the shadows.  nice choice of colour behind her red hair.  maybe a little unsharp mask too, but that''s just my preference. well done.<br/>Pedro</td>', 'get her to take three steps away from the backdrop and get a backlight in there, and this is great.  a little space and shallow depth would separate her a bit, and i think that would be a plus, as well as losing some of the shadows.  nice choice of colour behind her red hair.  maybe a little unsharp mask too, but that''s just my preference. well done.Pedro', '2004-03-19 03:10:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(628279, 64566, 10084, '<td valign="top">Absolutely hilarious. Excellent capture. Great depth of field. The child really stands out from the background. "10"</td>', 'Absolutely hilarious. Excellent capture. Great depth of field. The child really stands out from the background. "10"', '2004-03-19 03:24:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(628299, 64402, 6771, '<td valign="top">Very good gray scales and lighting with focus spot on.   The angle just makes her left eye look a little strange.  nice work</td>', 'Very good gray scales and lighting with focus spot on.   The angle just makes her left eye look a little strange.  nice work', '2004-03-19 03:58:45.000000', NULL, 1),
