(630761, 64514, 15360, '<td valign="top">This was my feeble attempt to experiment with Hedgecoe''s "Using Candlelight".  My original plan was to illuminate only the face.  Everything else is covered with garments.  That''s where things start to go wrong.  I adjusted the brightness/contrast until I could see only trace outlines of the garments.  I didn''t pay enough attention to others (including my other monitors ) that may not be able to calibrate their monitors to view the picture as I was seeing it.<br/> <br/>Add some cropping issues and likely an uninteresting picture to most people and the result seems predictable.<br/> <br/>Overall I''m happy with the picture.  I did what I set out to do and learned a lot from the experience.<br/> <br/>Thanks to all.</td>', 'This was my feeble attempt to experiment with Hedgecoe''s "Using Candlelight".  My original plan was to illuminate only the face.  Everything else is covered with garments.  That''s where things start to go wrong.  I adjusted the brightness/contrast until I could see only trace outlines of the garments.  I didn''t pay enough attention to others (including my other monitors ) that may not be able to calibrate their monitors to view the picture as I was seeing it. Add some cropping issues and likely an uninteresting picture to most people and the result seems predictable. Overall I''m happy with the picture.  I did what I set out to do and learned a lot from the experience. Thanks to all.', '2004-03-22 00:27:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(630763, 64463, 6349, '<td valign="top">Thought this would do much much better.  Great shot!</td>', 'Thought this would do much much better.  Great shot!', '2004-03-22 00:28:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(630765, 64327, 10055, '<td valign="top">Well what can I say.. Yes it''s more of a still life shot....but I like to be creative a bit when I didn''t have other resourses at the time. However, thank you for the higher votes for those who saw more than just a (non) portrait shot but, a creative way of seeing things. After nearly 14 years now, I haven''t viewd this scuplture in the way as pcody stated. thanks...:) Until next challenge, happy shooting.</td>', 'Well what can I say.. Yes it''s more of a still life shot....but I like to be creative a bit when I didn''t have other resourses at the time. However, thank you for the higher votes for those who saw more than just a (non) portrait shot but, a creative way of seeing things. After nearly 14 years now, I haven''t viewd this scuplture in the way as pcody stated. thanks...:) Until next challenge, happy shooting.', '2004-03-22 00:28:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(630766, 64527, 12661, '<td valign="top">Way to go Kiwi. Truth be told, when I first saw that photograph, I immediately thought of McCurry''s National Geographic shot. Very well done.</td>', 'Way to go Kiwi. Truth be told, when I first saw that photograph, I immediately thought of McCurry''s National Geographic shot. Very well done.', '2004-03-22 00:28:48.000000', NULL, 0),
