(2333122, 64166, 38549, '<td valign="top">Coley<br/>im sorry for the critique you recieved by a previous member, that wasnt to proffesional<br/> <br/>anyone who looks at your profile can tell you have won your fair share of ribbons, so i am going to take it that you purposly put the red in your photo. <br/> <br/>so what i am seeing is the light is bright on the top half and dark on the bottom<br/>it seem almost out of focus,<br/>the facial expression is great, and so is the hair<br/>the white shirt under the red doesnt really work either, <br/>over all, i like it, you didnt crop off the elbos to close, the image is centered and cropped well<br/> <br/>improvments: try and get even light throughout, the white shirt kinda take your attetion away<br/> <br/>sustains:<br/>good crop, its definetly colorful, <br/> <br/>good job, keep shootig, isntit just a blast.</td>', 'Coleyim sorry for the critique you recieved by a previous member, that wasnt to proffesional anyone who looks at your profile can tell you have won your fair share of ribbons, so i am going to take it that you purposly put the red in your photo.  so what i am seeing is the light is bright on the top half and dark on the bottomit seem almost out of focus,the facial expression is great, and so is the hairthe white shirt under the red doesnt really work either, over all, i like it, you didnt crop off the elbos to close, the image is centered and cropped well improvments: try and get even light throughout, the white shirt kinda take your attetion away sustains:good crop, its definetly colorful,  good job, keep shootig, isntit just a blast.', '2006-04-21 16:00:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(2703609, 64527, 11613, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by kiwiness:</b></div><hr/><i> Looking at this again after one and a half years, I now find that I don''t like this as much as I did when I submitted it. For one thing the light is too flat and the crop could also have been a lot better. I much prefer this version <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=268764" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/5728/thumb/268764.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/5728/thumb/268764.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/5728/thumb/268764.jpg"/></a> </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>The one you submitted is better. Just look at the eyes. The ayes have it. Everyone in agreement say aye. Also the submitted pic has less visible facial blemishes on the left side (her right).</td>', 'Originally posted by kiwiness: Looking at this again after one and a half years, I now find that I don''t like this as much as I did when I submitted it. For one thing the light is too flat and the crop could also have been a lot better. I much prefer this version    The one you submitted is better. Just look at the eyes. The ayes have it. Everyone in agreement say aye. Also the submitted pic has less visible facial blemishes on the left side (her right).', '2006-08-07 16:57:58.000000', NULL, 0),
